BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:$10 Off Tix: SF’s “Terror Vault” 1874 Halloween Haunt is Bac
 k (Oct. 1-Nov. 1)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261002T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261002T213000
DTSTAMP:20261006T001646Z
UID:funcheap-1636140@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theater Performance
DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event Organizer$10 Off Tix: SF’s “Terror 
 Vault” 1874 Halloween Haunt is Back for 2026 (Oct. 1-Nov. 1)San Francisc
 o’s premiere haunted attraction returns for 2026 with “SLASHED: Return
  to Hellville” an all-new\, bigger\, and more terrifying theatrical and 
 immersive experience from the insane mind of Peaches Christ.\nBrand new fo
 r 2026: Thirty-seven years after the infamous Hellville massacre\, a terri
 fying new evil has awakened. Step inside Terror Vault’s most ambitious i
 mmersive horror experience yet as you become trapped inside a living 1980s
  slasher movie. Journey through abandoned schools\, haunted campgrounds\, 
 blood-soaked fraternity houses\, forgotten video stores\, and other iconic
  horror locations while confronting a masked killer\, vengeful ghosts\, an
 d the terrifying legacy of Dr. Grieves’ Fear Engine. Featuring Hollywood
 -caliber sets\, cinematic storytelling\, live actors\, and pulse-pounding 
 scares\, SLASHED: Return to Hellville is more than a haunted attraction. I
 t’s a fully immersive horror adventure where every room is another scene
 \, every shadow hides a killer\, and every decision you make brings you cl
 oser to uncovering the mystery… or becoming its next victim. Enter Hellv
 ille. Escape if you can.\nThis goes waaay beyond just some regular haunted
  house. This is an hour-long immersive and theatrical experience which spa
 ns 3 floors of the building w/ 29 fully developed immersive sets and over 
 100 scare actors each night at the historic 1874 San Francisco Mint....\n\
 nFree\n\nTickets: https://www.terrorvault.com/\nDetails: https://sf.funche
 ap.com/10-off-tix-sfs-terror-vault-1874-halloween-haunt-is-back-oct-1-nov-
 1/\nSource: Funcheap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/09/427975
 51_174789190089978_7918193971669499904_n.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T001646Z
LOCATION:San Francisco Mint\, 5th St.\, San Francisco\, CA
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/10-off-tix-sfs-terror-vault-1874-halloween-hau
 nt-is-back-oct-1-nov-1/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Empty Pocket\, a Dance/Theater Work
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261002T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261002T223000
DTSTAMP:20261006T001646Z
UID:funcheap-1637105@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theater Performance
DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event OrganizerThe Empty Pocket\, created and
  performed by Heidi Carlsen\, is a surreal fairytale of a woman and a heir
 loom peacoat.\nTold through heightened imagery and poetry\, the piece foll
 ows a voyage where trust turns as unpredictable as a capricious ocean\, wh
 ere what once felt safe becomes threatening\, and where freedom is denied 
 by authority’s version of reality. Against that fear\, she crosses the f
 orbidden line\, breaking the silence and daring to speak up.\n\nLighting D
 esign\, Joyce Liao. Media Artist Nanda D’Agostino. Dramaturgical and Dir
 ectorial support: Mary Armentrout and Belinda He.\n\n$20.00\n\nTickets: ht
 tps://joegoode.org/event/heidi-carlsen-presents-the-empty-pocket-a-new-dan
 ce-theater-work/\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/empty-pocket-dancetheat
 er-work/\nSource: Funcheap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/TEP_SO
 CIAL_1080X1080.png
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T001646Z
LOCATION:Joe Goode Annex\, 401 Alabama\, San Francisco\, CA
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/empty-pocket-dancetheater-work/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Filipino Island Fest (Alameda)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T200000
DTSTAMP:20261006T001646Z
UID:funcheap-1632769@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theater Performance
DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event OrganizerOne of the largest Filipino cu
 ltural events returns to the Alameda waterfront for a 3rd year on Saturday
 \, October 3rd\, 2026. Filipino Island Fest brings thousands of attendees 
 together to celebrate Filipino culture\, community\, and belonging.\nThis 
 year’s theme reflects both where Filipinos come from and where they stan
 d today: “Rooted Here – Culture That Grounds Us. Community That Grows 
 Us.”\n\nGrounded in the spirit of Bayanihan\, it honors the connections\
 , traditions\, and collective strength that continue to shape Filipino ide
 ntity and future. The festival features different activations highlighting
  Filipino heritage\, wellness\, sports\, artisans\, performances\, and foo
 d from across the diaspora.\n️ Early Bird Admission — $5\n\nAvailable 
 for the first 5\,000 tickets sold.\n\n️ General Admission — $10\nFesti
 val Supporter Pass — $20 (Limited)\n\nBest Value — Same price as Day-O
 f Admission\, plus exclusive festival perks when purchased in advance.\nFe
 stival admission\nLimited edition Filipino Island Fest tote bag\nExpress e
 ntry lane\nExpress bar lane\n\n️ Day-Of Admission — $20\n\nFestival ad
 mission only.\n\n✨ VIP Experience — $125\n\nVIP lounge access\nCatered
  Filipino food\nComplimentary drink\nReserved seating\nPrivate bar\nPremiu
 m restroom access\n\nFor children under 5 years & seniors over 65 years.\n
 Every ticket purchased helps support Filipino artists\, musicians\, perfor
 mers\, small businesses\, cultural programming\, and the continued growth 
 of one of the largest Filipino cultu...\n\n$5.00\n\nTickets: https://www.f
 ilipinoislandfest.com/\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/filipino-island-f
 est-alameda/\nSource: Funcheap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Filipi
 no-Island-Fest-2026.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T001646Z
LOCATION:2151 Ferry Point Alameda\, CA 94501
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/filipino-island-fest-alameda/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Free 30-Minute Dance Shows on Freedom + Justice at SF Libraries (O
 ct. 3-17)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T133000
DTSTAMP:20261006T001646Z
UID:funcheap-1638701@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theater Performance
DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event OrganizerOctober 3 – 17: Shows at 1pm
  and 3:15pm each Saturday\nFlyaway Productions returns to the streets with
  a new dance-based public art project exploring the concept of freedom at 
 the intersection of public libraries and prisons. Directed by Flyaway Arti
 stic Director Jo Kreiter in coalition with the San Francisco Public Librar
 y\, ‘Freedom Comes’ features a cast of seven female dancers\, original
  research and text by April Harris\, and commissioned music by Kalyn Harwo
 od.\n\nA total of six 30-minute shows are scheduled at 1 p.m. and 3:15 p.m
 . over three consecutive Saturdays\, October 3 – 17. ‘Freedom Comes’
  opens October 3 at Visitacion Valley Branch Library before moving to the 
 San Francisco Main Library on October 10\, and finally to the Ortega Branc
 h Library on October 17. All shows are free with no reservation required.\
 nFlyaway’s primary collaborator is April Harris\, an incarcerated writer
  serving a life sentence at the California Institution for Women in Corona
 \, California. She is currently a research advocate to support the Univers
 ity of California Sentencing Project\, a collaboration between the Univers
 ity of California at San Diego and Los Angeles\, and members of the Califo
 rnia Coalition of Women Prisoners.\nAccording to the Sentencing Project\, 
 between 1980 and 2022\, the number of incarcerated women surged nearly six
 -fold\, with Black women imprisoned at rates 60% higher than white women. 
 In the U.S.\, the flow of information between those who are inca...\n\nFre
 e\n\nTickets: http://flyawayproductions.com\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.
 com/free-30minute-dance-shows-freedom-justice-sf-libraries-oct-317/\nSourc
 e: Funcheap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/4730_v
 0.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T001646Z
LOCATION:Visitacion Valley Branch Library (plus 2 other SF locations)\, 20
 1 Leland Ave\, San Francisco\, CA 94134
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/free-30minute-dance-shows-freedom-justice-sf-l
 ibraries-oct-317/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Paul Sussman’s Did She Really Say “Tantrum Yoga?”
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T181000
DTSTAMP:20261006T001646Z
UID:funcheap-1639675@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theater Performance
DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event Organizer\nThe world is reeling towards
  chaos! Wars! Fires! Corruption! The Death of Democracy! It’s an all-out
  Emergency!!! THIS TIME IS DIFFERENT! It’s time to get out of denial\, s
 tare down the grim reality\, and… party? There’s nothing like an encou
 nter with a mysterious stranger at a party: take a risk\, lay yourself bar
 e\, and – just maybe – find a tiny bit of hope and laughter amidst the
  chaos. Paul Sussman’s latest creation tosses us into the center of the 
 swirl\, and offers us lifelines to laugh\, to cry\, to hope\, and to act.\
 n70 minutes | No intermission | Ages 13+ (Please do not bring infants to t
 he show)\n\nTickets: $25 – $35 General Seating | $50 & $100 Reserved Sea
 ting\nLearn more: https://cbpr.co/press/didshejustsaytantrumyoga/\n\n$25.0
 0\n\nTickets: https://eventvesta.com/events/163592/t/tickets\nDetails: htt
 ps://sf.funcheap.com/paul-sussmans-tantrum-yoga/\nSource: Funcheap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/unname
 d-5.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T001646Z
LOCATION:The Marsh (San Francisco Mainstage)\, 1062 Valencia Street San F
 rancisco\, CA 94110
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/paul-sussmans-tantrum-yoga/
END:VEVENT
