BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:FOSS: an immersive live audiovisual experience
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261016T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261016T213000
DTSTAMP:20261006T001200Z
UID:dothebay-17843536@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theatre & Performing Arts
DESCRIPTION:FOSS is an immersive live audiovisual experience where electro
 nic music\, cinematic visuals\, and cutting-edge technology converge. Crea
 ted by Grammy-nominated pianist and composer Romain Collin and producer/el
 ectronic musician Jeremy Loucas\, the performance grew from Collin’s six
 -month artistic retreat in the remote Icelandic highlands\, where silence\
 , vast landscapes\, and isolation inspired a striking new creative vision.
 \n\nPerformed entirely live using modular synthesizers\, tape machines\, k
 eyboards\, and custom analog instruments—with no pre-recorded tracks—F
 OSS surrounds audiences with richly layered ambient soundscapes\, projecti
 on-mapped visuals\, and a quadraphonic sound system. The result is a mesme
 rizing\, genre-defying performance that blurs the boundaries between music
 \, film\, nature\, and technology.\n\nLearn more at fossfossfoss.com\n\n$3
 5\n\nTickets: https://gracecathedral.vbotickets.com/event/FOSS_an_immersiv
 e_live_audiovisual_experience/203642?utm_source=dothebay&utm_medium=calend
 ar&utm_campaign=foss\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/16/foss
 -an-immersive-live-audiovisual-experience-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/34424778/9d01bfac-4e84-49af-b11b-54aafecfb39c.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T001200Z
LOCATION:Grace Cathedral\, 1100 California Street\, San Francisco\, CA\, 9
 4108
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/16/foss-an-immersive-live-audiovis
 ual-experience-tickets
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Gummo
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261016T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261016T213000
DTSTAMP:20261006T001200Z
UID:dothebay-17884756@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theatre & Performing Arts
DESCRIPTION:Harmony Korine’s debut feature is an audacious\, lyrical evo
 cation of America’s rural underbelly\, and an elegy in the southern-goth
 ic tradition of William Faulkner and William Eggleston. Shot in Korine’s
  native Nashville—standing in for the tornado-ravaged Xenia\, Ohio—the
  rough-hewn film follows two young friends\, Tummler and Solomon\, as they
  ride around town\, huffing glue and hunting stray cats\, their every loca
 l encounter charged with vaudevillian anarchy as well as deep pathos. At o
 nce transgressive and empathetic\, disturbing and undeniably beautiful\, G
 ummo is a one-of-a-kind portrait of angelic and devilish souls caught in a
  cultural void\, circumscribed by poverty and the depleted\, alienated spi
 ritual life of late-twentieth-century America.\n\nThis film can be used wi
 th loyalty cards or our 2026 annual CinemaSFBay passes\n\nTickets: https:/
 /ticketing.uswest.veezi.com/purchase/19984?siteToken=52wkfzmjpwjjfpz3ye7tz
 8wscg\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/16/gummo-tickets\nSour
 ce: DoTheBay
GEO:37.7760419;-122.498063
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/34623009/8c04904e-8a12-4445-8138-7ab6678a7e49.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T001200Z
LOCATION:Balboa Theater\, 3630 Balboa St\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94121
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/16/gummo-tickets
END:VEVENT
